$DIR/main.p:13:2: cannot pass arr[:] to vec.(*Vec).Push, which keeps it after returning
    arr[:] is a slice that looks at arr. arr is a local array of f (declared at
    main.p:12). vec.(*Vec).Push passes x to rt.InitValue (vec.p:152), which
    stores it in memory another argument points to, so arr[:] would outlive arr.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    If vec.(*Vec).Push should keep its own copy of arr, change it to take the
    value, not a pointer, or an owner it can keep: an owned[[2]int] from new, a
    shared[[2]int], or a library owner such as a vec.Vec.
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3003" for a longer explanation)
